    "title": "Scattered showers expected again with cold front coming Wednesday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Bianca Thomas ,\n15 hours ago Shown in this photo is a crossing guard assists Pietzch-MacArthur students as they cross Highland Avenue in a late afternoon rainfall Wednesday. Photo made Wednesday, April 14, 2021 Kim Brent/The Enterprise (Kim Brent/The Enterprise) Another rainy day is expected for Southeast Texans in Wednesday's weather forecast.\nRain chances ramp up to 80% today as a cold front approaches and moves across the region. The front also brings a marginal risk for excessive rainfall, severe weather and damaging winds, according to the National Weather Service Lake Charles.\nShowers and thunderstorms are expected before 2 p.m. and after 4 p.m. These storms could produce heavy rainfall. Areas south of Interstate 10 in Beaumont will see the most rain. Fog is also expected between 7 a.m. and 9 a.m.\nAside from the showers, skies will be partly sunny with temperatures in the high 90s and a heat index near 103, the NWS daily forecast said.\nCalm winds are expected to shift southwest at around 5 mph in the morning. Showers and thunderstorms are also expected in the evening, with a 90% chance of precipitation. Overnight temperatures will be in the low 70s.\nSign up for Beaumont Enterprise newsletters here\nRead the original article on beaumontenterprise.com\n16",
